Subject: [PATCH] llvm-profile: define bitmap statics for "Other" platforms

The compiler-rt profile runtime in this LLVM tree carries the MC/DC-era
bitmap accessors in InstrProfilingPlatformOther.c
(__llvm_profile_begin_bitmap / __llvm_profile_end_bitmap) but not the
BitmapFirst/BitmapLast statics they return, so platforms using the
generic fallback (e.g. QNX) fail to compile the profiler runtime:

  InstrProfilingPlatformOther.c: 'BitmapFirst' undeclared
  InstrProfilingPlatformOther.c: 'BitmapLast' undeclared

Upstream llvm-project defines both statics in this file (initialized to
NULL and never updated by __llvm_profile_register_function - the bitmap
region stays empty on registration-based platforms). This backports
exactly that: profile counters (line/function/branch coverage) work,
MC/DC bitmaps are a no-op, matching upstream behavior.

Replaces the stale hand-written patches/llvm-qnx-profiler-bitmap.patch,
which additionally implemented bitmap bookkeeping in the registration
function (beyond upstream, only needed for MC/DC on QNX) and was not in
the scripted patch path (scripts/patches/) nor appliable with git apply.

---
--- a/src/llvm-project/compiler-rt/lib/profile/InstrProfilingPlatformOther.c
+++ b/src/llvm-project/compiler-rt/lib/profile/InstrProfilingPlatformOther.c
@@ -27,6 +27,8 @@ static const char *VNamesFirst = NULL;
 static const char *VNamesLast = NULL;
 static char *CountersFirst = NULL;
 static char *CountersLast = NULL;
+static char *BitmapFirst = NULL;
+static char *BitmapLast = NULL;
 
 static const void *getMinAddr(const void *A1, const void *A2) {
   return A1 < A2 ? A1 : A2;
